Source: seine
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Cedric Hombourger <chombourger@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               dh-python,
               python3-all,
               python3-setuptools
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/chombourger/seine
X-Python3-Version: >= 3.11

Package: seine
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         ansible,
         crun,
         passt,
         podman,
         python3-guestfs,
         qemu-kvm
Recommends: gnupg
Suggests: qemu-user-static
Description: slim embedded images, now easy
 seine builds bootable images (disk images, rootfs tarballs, containers)
 from a YAML specification, using podman to run each build step in a
 throwaway container and libguestfs to write the result to its final
 image format.
 .
 This package provides the seine command line tool.

Package: seine-oci-bookworm-amd64
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: seine (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: seine-oci-bookworm-arm64, seine-oci-trixie-arm64
Description: prebuilt debian:bookworm base image for amd64 hosts
 The 'debian:bookworm' image for an amd64 host, imported into podman on
 first use instead of pulled from a registry -- the only image any of
 seine's own container builds ever pull rather than build locally.
 Install alongside seine-oci-trixie-amd64 for both releases; not
 alongside an arm64 host package.

